{"d":25,"passage":{"title":"雾都孤儿","author":"Charles Dickens","text":"It was impossible to doubt him; there was truth in every one of its thin and sharpened lineaments. But, although his motive for looking steadily at Oliver no longer existed, the old idea of the resemblance between his features and some familiar face came upon him so strongly, that he could not withdraw his gaze. As he spoke, he pointed hastily to the picture over Oliver's head, and then to the boy's face. The expression was, for the instant, so precisely alike, that the minutest line seemed copied with startling accuracy! Oliver knew not the cause of this sudden exclamation; for, not being strong enough to bear the start it gave him, he fainted away. A weakness on his part, which affords the narrative an opportunity of relieving the reader from suspense, in behalf of the two young pupils of the Merry Old Gentleman; and of recording— For, these are matters totally beneath a female who is acknowledged by universal admission to be far above the numerous little foibles and weaknesses of her sex."},"words":[{"w":"yeah","uk":"jɑː","us":"/jɑ/","p":"","m":"adv. (非正式)是, 是的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null,"b2":null},{"w":"javascript","uk":"","us":"","p":"","m":"n. Java描述语言（一种程序语言）","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null,"b2":null},{"w":"advisor","uk":"əd'vaizə","us":"/əd'vaizə/","p":"","m":"n. 顾问, 劝告者, 指导教师","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null,"b2":{"r":"Proverbs 24:6","c":"箴言 24:6","t":"for by wise guidance you wage your war, and victory is in many advisors."}},{"w":"marketplace","uk":"'mɑːkit'pleis","us":"/'mɑkit'pleis/","p":"","m":"n. 市场","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":{"r":"Matthew 20:3","c":"马太福音 20:3","t":"And he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the marketplace, 20:4 And said unto them; Go ye also into the vineyard, and whatsoever is right I will give you. And they went their way."},"b2":{"r":"Mark 12:38","c":"马可福音 12:38","t":"In his teaching he said 